  "result": "Done! Added VAT calculations per line and updated invoice totals and rendering.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **VAT calculation logic** \u2014 In invoiceTotals():\n   - VAT is calculated per line on the amount **after discount**\n   - Line VAT = roundCents((lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100)\n   - Invoice VAT is the **sum of rounded line VATs**, never a percentage of invoice total\n   - This ensures precision and handles different VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%) per line\n\n2. **Updated invoiceTotals()** \u2014 Now returns { subtotal, discount, vat, total }:\n   - **subtotal**: sum of all line totals\n   - **discount**: sum of all line discounts\n   - **vat**: sum of all calculated line VATs\n   - **total**: subtotal - discount + vat, clamped to \u2265 0\n\n3. **Updated renderInvoiceText()** \u2014 Shows VAT on invoice:\n   - Displays \"VAT: \u20acX.XX\" line above the total (only if VAT > 0)\n   - Uses invoiceTotals() to get precise calculations\n   - Total line shows final amount including VAT\n\n4. **Test coverage** \u2014 9 new tests:\n   - VAT on discounted amount\n   - Multiple VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n   - VAT with mixed discounts\n   - Rendering with/without VAT\n   - VAT in totals calculation\n\n5. **Updated 6 existing tests** \u2014 To account for VAT in totals\n\nAll 95 tests pass (9 new VAT tests + 6 updated + 80 previous).\n\n**How it works:**\n- Line with 100 qty @ \u20ac100 unit price, 10% discount, 21% VAT:\n  - Line total: \u20ac10,000\n  - After discount (10%): \u20ac9,000\n  - VAT (21% of \u20ac9,000): \u20ac1,890\n  - Line contribution to total: \u20ac10,000 - \u20ac1,000 + \u20ac1,890 = \u20ac10,890",
